################## Calculation params #############################
# Cluster (non-periodic) HSE06 + MBD-NL single-point Mulliken DOS.
#
# Derived from calculations/dos/control.in.template, which is the periodic slab
# version. Each A-J frame is a crop out of a larger TEM field of view and fills
# its cell almost exactly (A01 spans 44.1 A of a 45.41 A cell), so under
# periodic boundary conditions the crop rim bonds to its own image at an
# arbitrary registry: 13-24 bonds per frame that exist only through the PBC, and
# 6-13 four-coordinate sp2 carbons that are not in the sheet. Because the shape
# changes from frame to frame while the cell does not, that artefact varies
# along the A->J series and contaminates the very trend being measured.
#
# The geometry.in staged alongside this file therefore carries no lattice_vector
# lines, which is how FHI-aims is told the structure is a cluster.
#
# Differences from the periodic template, all forced by dropping periodicity:
#   - k_grid / override_kgrid_checks removed. A cluster has a single k-point.
#     Little is lost: 2x2x1 on a 45 A cell was already close to Gamma-only.
#   - periodic_hf thresholds removed. They configure the lattice sum in the
#     exact-exchange evaluation and have no meaning without a lattice.
#   - RI_method LVL_fast set explicitly. Non-periodic hybrids in FHI-aims
#     otherwise default to RI-V, whose memory footprint is the practical limit
#     at the ~540 atoms these clusters reach.
#
# There is one further consequence of dropping periodicity that cannot be
# expressed in this file at all, and that decides which ARCHER2 partition the
# job must use:
#
#   read_control.f90 refuses 'use_local_index' whenever
#       use_hartree_fock .and. .not. use_periodic_hf
#   and use_periodic_hf is (use_hartree_fock .and. n_periodic > 0), so every
#   cluster hybrid trips it. Setting RI_method LVL_fast above does NOT satisfy
#   the check despite the error text mentioning LVL -- the condition keys on
#   periodicity, not on the RI method.
#
# Without use_local_index each MPI rank holds the full global sparse H and S:
# 100 GB per node at 128 ranks/node for D10, against ~0 GB for the periodic run
# of the same structure. Cluster jobs therefore run on highmem (446 GB) nodes;
# see the memory note in jobs/archer2_dos_cluster_array.slurm. Do not assume a
# cluster frame is cheaper than its periodic counterpart just because the k-sum
# is gone -- the exchange is cheaper, but the pre-SCF allocation is far worse.
#
# Everything else is deliberately unchanged from the periodic template so the
# cluster and periodic DOS remain comparable.

### XC-functional
xc                           hse06 0.11
hse_unit                     bohr
many_body_dispersion_nl      beta=0.81

### Resolution of identity
# See header: RI-V is the non-periodic default and is memory-bound at this size.
RI_method                    LVL_fast

### Relativistic
relativistic                 atomic_zora scalar

### Spin
# Closed shell for every cluster frame, matching the periodic batch. This is an
# imposed constraint, not a tested one: an odd valence-electron count cannot be
# closed shell at all, and a near-zero gap means the singlet is not the right
# reference either. Spin-collinear staging was tried and abandoned on cost - D10
# was still climbing in moment (0.01 -> 6.0 mu_B) at SCF iteration 137 when it
# hit the walltime. scripts/dos/stage_cluster_dos_calculations.py records which
# frames the assumption is poor for in results/tables/cluster_dos_staging.csv.
spin                         none
#default_initial_moment       0.01
#charge                       0.0

### Orbital construction
# Gaussian smearing is retained: a finite cluster has discrete levels, and
# several of these frames come out of GFN2 with a near-zero HOMO-LUMO gap, so
# the SCF needs the smearing to be stable.
occupation_type              gaussian 0.1
charge_mix_param             0.2
preconditioner               kerker 1.0

### Calculation type
# Single-point DOS evaluation only. The hydrogens were already relaxed with
# GFN2-xTB (scripts/mlip/relax_clusters_xtb.py) and the carbon backbone is held
# at the experimental TEM coordinates on purpose.
#relax_geometry              bfgs 1e-2

basis_threshold              1d-5
override_illconditioning     .true.

output mulliken

### SCF settings
sc_accuracy_etot                   1e-06
sc_accuracy_eev                    0.01
sc_accuracy_rho                    1e-05
sc_iter_limit                      1000

################ Atomic Environments ######################
# C/H-only control.in - every PDOS batch target contains only C and H.
################################################################################


################################################################################
#
#  FHI-aims code project
#  Volker Blum, Fritz Haber Institute Berlin, 2009
#
#  Suggested "tight" defaults for C atom
#
################################################################################

  species        C

    nucleus             6
    mass                12.0107

    l_hartree           6

    cut_pot             4.0  2.0  1.0
    basis_dep_cutoff    1e-4

    radial_base         34 7.0
    radial_multiplier   2
    angular_grids specified
      division   0.2187   50
      division   0.4416  110
      division   0.6335  194
      division   0.7727  302
      division   0.8772  434
#      division   0.9334  590
#      division   0.9924  770
#      division   1.0230  974
#      division   1.5020 1202
#     outer_grid  974
      outer_grid  434

################################################################################
#  Definition of "minimal" basis
################################################################################

    valence      2  s   2.
    valence      2  p   2.

    ion_occ      2  s   1.
    ion_occ      2  p   1.

################################################################################
#  Suggested additional basis functions
################################################################################

#  "First tier" - improvements: -1214.57 meV to -155.61 meV
     hydro 2 p 1.7
     hydro 3 d 6
     hydro 2 s 4.9

#  "Second tier" - improvements: -67.75 meV to -5.23 meV
     hydro 4 f 9.8
     hydro 3 p 5.2
     hydro 3 s 4.3
     hydro 5 g 14.4
     hydro 3 d 6.2

#  "Third tier" - improvements: -2.43 meV to -0.60 meV
#     hydro 2 p 5.6
#     hydro 2 s 1.4
#     hydro 3 d 4.9
#     hydro 4 f 11.2

#  "Fourth tier" - improvements: -0.39 meV to -0.18 meV
#     hydro 2 p 2.1
#     hydro 5 g 16.4
#     hydro 4 d 13.2
#     hydro 3 s 13.6
#     hydro 4 f 17.6

#  Further basis functions - improvements: -0.08 meV and below
#     hydro 3 s 2
#     hydro 3 p 6
#     hydro 4 d 20

################################################################################
#  Optional auxiliary basis for hybrid calculations
################################################################################
# for_aux hydro 5 g 6.0


################################################################################
#
#  FHI-aims code project
#  Volker Blum, Fritz Haber Institute Berlin, 2009
#
#  Suggested "tight" defaults for H atom
#
################################################################################

  species        H

    nucleus             1
    mass                1.00794

    l_hartree           6

    cut_pot             4.0  2.0  1.0
    basis_dep_cutoff    1e-4

    radial_base         24 7.0
    radial_multiplier   2
    angular_grids       specified
      division   0.1930   50
      division   0.3175  110
      division   0.4293  194
      division   0.5066  302
      division   0.5626  434
#      division   0.5922  590
#      division   0.6227  974
#      division   0.6868 1202
#      outer_grid  770
      outer_grid  434

################################################################################
#  Definition of "minimal" basis
################################################################################

    valence      1  s   1.

    ion_occ      1  s   0.5

################################################################################
#  Suggested additional basis functions
################################################################################

#  "First tier" - improvements: -1014.90 meV to -62.69 meV
     hydro 2 s 2.1
     hydro 2 p 3.5

#  "Second tier" - improvements: -12.89 meV to -1.83 meV
     hydro 1 s 0.85
     hydro 2 p 3.7
     hydro 2 s 1.2
     hydro 3 d 7

#  "Third tier" - improvements: -0.25 meV to -0.12 meV
#     hydro 4 f 11.2
#     hydro 3 p 4.8
#     hydro 4 d 9
#     hydro 3 s 3.2

################################################################################
#  Optional auxiliary basis for hybrid calculations
################################################################################
# for_aux hydro 5 g 6.0
